      {
        "id": "intro-comment",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Black and White, Hard\n\nConverts an image to pure black and white with a slightly soft edge. Converting to grayscale first means the threshold works on brightness, not on whichever colour channel dominates.\n\n**How it works:** \"1 Image\" takes the picture. \"2 Grayscale\" removes colour, and \"3 Threshold\" splits pixels at 0.55 with a softness of 0.03. \"4 Result\" shows the two-tone image. It runs locally with no model or key.\n\n**Try this:** Lower threshold on \"3 Threshold\" to 0.4 to keep more white, or raise softness to 0.1 for a gentler edge."
        },
